Many birds spread oil from a gland near the tail over their feathers during preening, helping maintain their plumage.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7795-8d19-bfe617fba206","description":"Preening","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7ead-872a-04202b206f3e","description":"Sweening","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-795a-be0f-be686674da2f","description":"Greening","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-781f-bab4-bda55f9efe01","description":"Feening","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-76a2-bdd0-691f2bb2ca69","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the sum of 1+2+3+4+5?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The sum is 15: the pairs 1+5 and 2+4 each total 6, and adding the middle term, 3, gives the result.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7752-a857-50560b66e1b1","description":"15","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-78b7-b803-552cdee012b6","description":"9","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7c93-ae7c-fdcbe69976df","description":"10","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-70cb-9602-41a182b0a902","description":"14","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7f44-b445-4641541888c1","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is Rhinology the study of?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Rhinology studies the nose and its diseases. The name combines a Greek root for the nose with -logy, meaning study.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7087-ac0b-14f7441a8653","description":"the nose and its diseases","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-78ca-8bba-1be48207793e","description":"ants","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7de4-8c5b-515360ce7d5c","description":"origin of life","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7e43-ac0e-e6d19d7d5673","description":"the age of trees and the records in their rings","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7578-95f0-4072d1fecbc7","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What are the 2 parts of complex numbers known as?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"In a + bi, a is the real part, while b is the coefficient of the imaginary unit i.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-799d-85dd-1366af608866","description":"Real & Imaginary","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-77e9-80c2-1c8b68e64a69","description":"True & False","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7312-beb4-b3887e0abe22","description":"Big & Small","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-71ec-91e6-da88fbd2b448","description":"Logical & Intuitive","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-74b7-9c3a-79c656da134b","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which Soviet spacecraft carried the dog Laika into orbit in 1957?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Laika became the first animal to orbit Earth aboard Sputnik 2, but she did not return alive.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7989-956c-f86ef294cc81","description":"Sputnik 2","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7084-b9d0-81ae823107ef","description":"Sputnik 1","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7895-83df-3678ec88cecb","description":"Vostok 1","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-74a2-839e-031cd4691574","description":"Luna 2","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7883-aa95-094e23603920","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the smallest bird in the world?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The Bee Hummingbird is native to Cuba, and females are slightly larger than males.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7961-8db3-615cd10a9a70","description":"Bee Hummingbird","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7c4d-b951-3a6bcc589a28","description":"Pigeon","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-79b7-9adf-f7f4b02338a7","description":"Great Horned Owl","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7e78-b549-2ae187ce3231","description":"Ostrich","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7e65-82ab-2d314e8983a7","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What infectious lung disease is known by two letters?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"TB stands for tuberculosis, a bacterial infection that most often affects the lungs and can spread through the air.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7a3b-875c-1b796d54f72e","description":"TB","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-773f-9354-b966607d13f7","description":"HF","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7e4d-a2a8-b2ce3a08b3f8","description":"CC","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7fa4-a116-888bd189e1df","description":"AK","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7e24-9e6b-44e6e204c152","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is Venereology the study of?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Venereology is the study of sexually transmitted diseases. Its name is related to \u201cvenereal,\u201d a term historically associated with Venus, the Roman goddess of love.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7430-bb62-6896e68f2a99","description":"Sexually transmitted diseases","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7592-a561-2ce6f520907e","description":"Vocal sounds","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-798b-b985-caaca1ad106c","description":"Grasshoppers and crickets","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-79a5-a094-7e259afa36a2","description":"Ants","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7a8e-99be-2a7dcb55987d","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What upward force acts on an object that is immersed in fluid?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The buoyant force follows Archimedes\' principle: its magnitude equals the weight of the fluid displaced by the immersed object.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7e35-8297-c77ecb0431e2","description":"Buoyant force","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-732c-8d03-07a329569cf6","description":"Shear force","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-720a-914e-2ab6853a1c86","description":"Viscous force","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7b8c-b7f1-edbf340185c9","description":"Drag force","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7136-aab9-496e2978d6d5","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"In laboratory settings, what word is used to refer to the act of stirring or shaking a liquid?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Agitating a liquid helps distribute its contents or resuspend settled material; a vortex mixer does this rapidly.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7d93-b9b5-15afa744049d","description":"Agitate","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7eeb-aff2-9857b492a32a","description":"Oscillate","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7c4e-b1c8-0333875647a0","description":"Dilute","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-738f-8f98-ce0e780f4742","description":"Tremble","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-75f3-90d4-703117e2dbd8","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"In 1898, which noble gas was discovered and named after the Greek word for \'hidden\'?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Krypton makes up only a tiny fraction of Earth\'s atmosphere, so it had to be isolated from liquefied air.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7b37-9e27-fd67e784752b","description":"Krypton","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7297-815d-bdcfdac64d8f","description":"Argon","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7421-bf94-7b5aa814b2fe","description":"Helium","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-797b-a8f3-b7c377e155ed","description":"Xenon","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-74fa-870b-d503a9f47c95","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the chemical mercury often used for?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Mercury is liquid at room temperature and expands predictably as it warms, making it useful in measuring instruments. Its toxicity has led to safer replacements in many applications.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-772d-a99f-e15cd78f5111","description":"It is used in thermometers, thermostats, barometers","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7f7d-ade8-6efb20310b8e","description":"It is used as an ingredient in baking.","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-705a-bb4d-a9ec1bdd983d","description":"It is used as an ingredient in the production of glass, bricks, and ceramics.","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7b04-8d06-fb3d8100b197","description":"It is used in disinfectants and antiseptics.","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-72ed-8de3-818e0d5890af","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the word for a group of owls?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"A parliament of owls is the established collective noun. The same word names a legislative assembly, giving the phrase a stately tone.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7ec8-a97a-6ccea3c6e525","description":"A parliament","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7087-be32-dd05df667f96","description":"A host","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7ad2-a768-953ae1b0e1f3","description":"A nest","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7ced-8cff-7e9a9277bb94","description":"A yoke","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7759-aca7-8c854bf1420c","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is Hypnology the study of?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Sleep research distinguishes REM and non-REM stages by patterns of brain activity and eye movements.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7c5a-86b5-e9215af6ebe6","description":"Sleep","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7365-b2f1-e65af8fb94b6","description":"Radiation","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7f4a-a31e-ff70a0a50343","description":"Earth materials","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-76a9-be22-2c3135829018","description":"The eyes","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-770b-aa1b-478a129a5413","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the word for a young termite?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Termites undergo incomplete metamorphosis, so young hatch as nymphs that resemble small adults.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-705f-aee2-a927d09777e9","description":"A Nymph","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7511-a577-13bf2d7338c9","description":"An Elver","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-755d-ae9d-edc82f2d729f","description":"A Kitten","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-77af-a354-08953d10d1d6","description":"An Owlet","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7074-a448-5d77a53642ec","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is Pathology the study of?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Pathology investigates the causes and effects of illness. Pathologists often examine tissue, blood, and other samples to help diagnose conditions.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7aa5-a305-f59414f3196e","description":"illness","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-72c4-a0d5-3e93bd81bc73","description":"the classical Chinese literary masterpiece Dream of the Red Chamber","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7465-868d-3f38b5df8ffb","description":"the practice of escaping from restraints or other traps","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-780f-8d1a-960284f9dd82","description":"fermentation","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7fb5-801c-9bd63395ffa6","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Who invented dynamite?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Alfred Nobel patented dynamite in 1867, and his will provided for the prizes that bear his name.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7d4c-b8f9-0a71749a0f3a","description":"Alfred Nobel","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7714-aa47-198c98fbeee9","description":"Nikola Tesla","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7e0b-926c-162f150d28c1","description":"Thomas Edison","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7173-a9e3-7ed07dcbc4b5","description":"Leonardo da Vinci","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7479-b593-9c6070b53f03","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the SI unit of pressure?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The pascal is named after Blaise Pascal, a French mathematician and physicist who studied pressure.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7e95-828d-343a847e9aa8","description":"Pascal","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7e59-9919-2755b570df86","description":"Newton","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7427-9eac-afb0dc5bee2b","description":"Joule","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-77c1-ba2a-95c6d6b9bb56","description":"Watt","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7339-bbe4-81af800c40f9","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the largest species of penguin?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The emperor penguin is the largest living penguin and breeds during the Antarctic winter.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-77f9-946e-f8e00c91b32a","description":"Emperor","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7664-9e85-f6b696f932e9","description":"King","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7995-8d2e-89792b6c5e7f","description":"Gentoo","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-703e-924a-e9f3caab14dd","description":"Ad\u00e9lie","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-78b2-8942-800e60f1685f","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the word for a young mule?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"A foal is the young of a horse or donkey. A mule is the hybrid offspring of a male donkey and a female horse.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7e42-8333-cb510df74f7f","description":"A Foal","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7183-8b6a-8efa30ee91af","description":"A Cria","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-720a-bef1-fbc600d98c2b","description":"A Bunny","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7664-868f-946752746e08","description":"A Lamb","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7eb5-a144-d0cff939aebe","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What name is often used to refer to a type of flying possum?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"A glider has a membrane of skin between its limbs that lets it travel between trees without powered flight.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7d40-b965-b01a2201b003","description":"A glider","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7569-b0fc-d26321df5334","description":"A leaper","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-72bf-aa95-056dc3ed07bf","description":"A flyer","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7871-ac59-f946a2388762","description":"A hanger","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7136-b868-b66d27508859","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is dry ice made of?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Carbon dioxide is called dry ice because it changes directly from a solid to a gas at ordinary pressure, without melting into a liquid.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-70a4-8907-e58155d93291","description":"Carbon dioxide","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7e71-a778-29a4d58b0fc5","description":"Nitrogen","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7ddb-aa7a-a26140adbf5d","description":"Oxygen","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7e2c-9cec-0e0cc3c9590d","description":"Methane","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-749f-84f7-848ecbab7328","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is Paleoanthropology the study of?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Paleoanthropology uses fossils and archaeological evidence to trace how hominins changed over time.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7efb-9f39-29a668bfac69","description":"prehistoric people and human origins","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7cd4-8ffb-72d9e9f9adaf","description":"interactions between organisms and geomorphological processes","correct_answer":false},{"id