mps, though severe outcomes are uncommon.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7e7d-ad30-478d7de268d0","description":"Black Widow","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7e21-beda-350c2689ac3e","description":"Brown Recluse","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-764d-8472-fff21c63245f","description":"Daddy Longlegs","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7d18-afc1-f6298ea575c9","description":"Tarantula","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-75ea-8e9c-8a1a754286b6","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which substance is quickly absorbed through the walls of the stomach?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Alcohol can pass into the bloodstream through the stomach lining, though most absorption occurs in the small intestine.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-789f-bb06-c8ee9457238b","description":"Alcohol","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7602-b829-9ea6524d68fd","description":"Butter","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7d18-a9e6-716d0923531c","description":"Olive oil","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7bed-a65d-ff9b2c7ff80a","description":"Ice cream","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-78a9-b5b2-c5a34420a0cc","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What gives flamingos their pink color?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Flamingos process carotenoids from algae and crustaceans and deposit them in their feathers, giving the feathers their pink hue.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-76d0-bf77-463ec1ed10fe","description":"Pigments from their food","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7605-9c4a-877b526e87e8","description":"Sunburn","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7780-b9ec-a6820dafc67a","description":"A pink-pigment gene","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-731d-8d5e-c8e242777175","description":"Minerals in the water","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae82-7331-af58-bec9d8eafd46","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868