a","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7943-8bd7-0b8cf036f7b7","description":"Tympanum","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7942-8d2c-3cfe93e8717a","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Who developed the theory of universal gravitation?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Isaac Newton presented the law of universal gravitation in his 1687 work Principia Mathematica, which also set out his laws of motion.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7f5a-b3c1-fbcaf9aadde7","description":"Isaac Newton","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7b69-bd96-75dda4a12a0d","description":"Albert Einstein","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7266-81c2-959db3de8ba3","description":"Charles Darwin","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7386-b4c2-0d50dee8d588","description":"Galileo Galilei","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7bc2-8071-0f21989a92c2","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What does a snake use to smell with?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"A snake\u2019s forked tongue collects chemical particles and brings them to the Jacobson\u2019s organ for analysis; snakes also detect odors through their nostrils.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7b1d-a4a8-042745f82ab8","description":"Tongue","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7b31-8be9-bf7da3bac02e","description":"Nose","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7e4a-813e-fe068fdcdb20","description":"Anus","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-72d1-94ee-110299ab2684","description":"Ears","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-71e9-b89a-1dfb69ab6a53","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which planet is third in mass and eighth from the sun?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Neptune was predicted from irregularities in Uranus\u2019s orbit before astronomers observed it in 1846.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7054-93c7-21b53899f9e3","description":"Neptune","correct_answer":true},{"id":"0