structure that sets a limit.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7086-8ae4-8cff450c2499","description":"Octopus","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7aa8-a0e5-37ac9d183597","description":"Seal","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-71c5-b7df-dd2453351ca7","description":"Sea otter","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7470-934f-24d98586f0e1","description":"Dolphin","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7e2c-a703-21a7f1d09c40","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which type of doctor specializes in surgery of the bones and joints?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Orthopedists (orthopedic surgeons) treat bone and joint disorders such as fractures and arthritis.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-78ff-b43f-8b1b47367133","description":"Orthopedist","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7ee0-bb92-d9c3014b2ec3","description":"Podiatrist","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7770-8b36-4592ae26c126","description":"Dermatologist","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7dc8-b1f6-8e83306f930d","description":"Cardiologist","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-78e9-be68-1dc9312b8998","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What number is the binary 1000000 equal to?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"64 is 2\u2076, so its binary form has a 1 in the 2\u2076 place and zeros in every lower place.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7889-8c67-063bcaa06909","description":"64","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7cb3-8633-656483a1fdff","description":"100","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7bd2-8766-f56797fc9229","description":"8","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7f02-97b1-86b302bb98e1","description":"50","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-717c-9cf2-8eff728eb5eb","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is Paleophytology the study of?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Paleophytology uses fossils to trace how vegetation changed through geological time.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7c69-ade6-900e42423baf","description":"ancient multicelled plants","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7f32-b9cb-1d56a2406e7f","description":"eggs","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-791c-9943-02a2cc73adc6","description":"the study, especially statistical, of elections","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7342-abb7-3d0ff516d206","description":"viruses","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-75ef-9ce1-6104e8acd520","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the other name for the Celsius temperature scale, meaning \"divided into one hundred parts\"?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Centigrade refers to the 100-degree interval between water\u2019s freezing and boiling points at standard atmospheric pressure.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7bb1-ae0c-fedd7a450d20","description":"Centigrade","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-72c0-b180-3f18b1515e91","description":"Fahrenheit","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-773e-bf95-c5b8503ffe25","description":"Kelvin","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7259-9dc0-e54bc5d58e4f","description":"Rankine","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7623-87a7-a1604b180437","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What adjective is attached to both Gustave Pasch\'s match and Walter Hunt\'s pin?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Safety matches keep key chemicals apart until striking, while a safety pin\'s clasp covers its sharp point.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-73f6-8171-2d1c04b3dcae","description":"Safety","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7f95-a047-b0a68b9d83e2","description":"Sharp","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7e0b-8a1d-17021bb6d653","description":"Smooth","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7d9e-860b-4ef4d80d0d94","description":"Bright","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7295-9fe5-3a9d6840deaf","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the tallest tree species in the world?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Coast redwoods can grow taller than 100 meters. Giant sequoias are generally shorter, though they are much bulkier.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7276-87d6-bc300cf39e94","description":"Coast Redwood","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7ee3-9dcd-a6bf04b25742","description":"Mountain Ash","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7524-8d15-25c30a455a3b","description":"Oak Tree","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7370-b4f9-7140437c4edd","description":"Douglas Fir","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7c26-a260-aefb2c2f10ab","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which fish is able to breathe air?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Lungfish have air-breathing organs, and some can survive drought buried in mud inside a mucus cocoon.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-783c-acf7-e662031ca374","description":"Lungfish","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-75fc-8b8a-51977b464d2b","description":"Shark","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-73a7-83ad-c43b1c699a1d","description":"Airfish","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7252-8c76-7b7f5d9c318a","description":"Bubblefish","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7efd-a10d-682585271900","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What are, on average, the heaviest primates?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Gorillas are the largest living primates. The name silverback refers to the pale hair that develops across a mature male\u2019s back.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-77cc-a555-045ffacd19a0","description":"Gorillas","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7ba7-81f0-9f4ba675a259","description":"Humans","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7923-a598-5ca2651520b8","description":"Orangutans","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7aa6-ae63-47c7be80b50a","description":"Chimpanzees","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7282-9343-89821297b474","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which is NOT a source of renewable energy?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Petroleum forms over geological timescales from buried organic matter, so it is finite. Biomass, sunlight, and tidal motion are replenished naturally.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7584-bbe7-3bb382e519cd","description":"Petroleum","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-77ac-b0aa-d058f6e76946","description":"Biomass","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-72a4-bf95-82a7847f372a","description":"Sun","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-791b-809b-2981a597bbc8","description":"Tides","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7ed2-a3c0-e9f471ca1333","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"If you were travelling at mach 2 how fast would you be travelling?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Mach number compares an object\'s velocity with the local speed of sound, so Mach 2 is double that reference velocity.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-77d9-b435-3be966103781","description":"Twice the speed of sound","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7ade-9179-a6cb269fac42","description":"Twice the speed of light","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7d7e-9f10-66f0cf507859","description":"200 miles per hour","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7e98-8911-d6868b8670bd","description":"2 miles per second","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7c5a-ae04-26c84fa891c0","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which of these scientific theories was an improvement over the theory of mechanics by Isaac Newton?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"General relativity extends Newtonian gravity and predicts that massive objects bend light, an effect confirmed by observations near the Sun.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7d8a-bd6c-5502be47548d","description":"General relativity","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-74e0-b208-75b83691d53e","description":"Lamarckism","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-791e-aece-5dcd8c122399","description":"Maxwell\'s equations","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-712b-8e16-7293269f60dc","description":"Snell\'s law","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7107-9c72-7a18745e4553","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"How many neck vertebrae does a giraffe have?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Seven is also the usual number of neck vertebrae in humans; giraffes\u2019 vertebrae are simply much longer.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7e76-af4a-03239bdfa2d5","description":"Seven","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7d9d-9bb4-d234fa220cfb","description":"Fourteen","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7637-a449-82d0d11a38b1","description":"Nine","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-78ff-b862-9896b9ebc745","description":"Twelve","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7042-891b-adf99076910c","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the word used when one tectonic plate moves under another?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Subduction can create deep ocean trenches and volcanic arcs, and it is associated with powerful earthquakes.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7366-b60b-f01fcb8e895a","description":"Subduction","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7e80-a9a0-0a0e49e78576","description":"Profession","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7e7c-95a1-f2a3b94fe5e9","description":"Induction","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-72ae-b079-23b2aa71e543","description":"Transgression","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7a29-b660-8f089d1c5c66","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Where in the body is the smallest human muscle?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The stapedius, the body\'s smallest skeletal muscle, is in the middle ear and helps limit the stapes\' movement in response to loud sounds.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7b41-8325-ef8ac2afc3a3","description":"Ear","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7ad8-97cd-960bf0051947","description":"Nose","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7a30-988e-da0a9101e6f1","description":"Hand","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-732c-be5a-f63a0fd8fec9","description":"Foot","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7f51-acf2-74ce399c8f88","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the specialty of an ophthalmologist?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Ophthalmologists are medical doctors who can perform surgery to treat conditions affecting the eyes.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7595-819a-9e449c6f77dc","description":"Eyes","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7100-afcb-7bc86cada8b8","description":"Testes","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7ae5-a447-3fea6f506494","description":"Kidneys","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7a29-bf3a-e21e4c02cfe3","description":"Feet","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-74f5-9d2e-7dc748a272b2","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"How many sides does a heptagon have?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The prefix hepta- comes from Greek for seven and also appears in heptathlon, an event with seven disciplines.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7fe1-8a76-acbbdefe2f01","description":"7","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7007-9433-10b6fc081c3b","description":"8","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-70e1-9278-7436cf632802","description":"6","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-73c0-924c-058df3ef6dc7","description":"9","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-77cd-a537-3ab3d6943e8c","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is Hierology the study of?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Hierology broadly concerns sacred matters, while theology focuses more specifically on God and religious doctrine.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7a49-90ae-34bba3a1f167","description":"a more inclusive term for theology","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-71ce-98db-cadcce230845","description":"the history, languages, and cultures of the Indian subcontinent","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-745d-a9ce-00652b32a22d","description":"the Sumerians","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-713e-8e08-6a7999ab6ade","description":"crayfish","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-79ae-b832-10b482e7c5bc","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which gas, produced by bacteria, forms the holes in Swiss cheese?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"In Swiss cheese, propionic acid bacteria release carbon dioxide as they ferment, and the trapped bubbles form the characteristic holes.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7451-ba83-191a1a3ccd81","description":"Carbon dioxide","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-77ba-89c5-fd891421a542","description":"Oxygen","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7113-b16c-175207f4232e","description":"Nitrogen","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7ca9-ab03-697ad1fda8af","description":"Methane","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-754b-ba29-9e0be75ee967","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the name of a triangle with two sides of equal length?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"An isosceles triangle has at least two sides of equal length; when all three sides match, it is also equilateral.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7b45-8044-caa07133106b","description":"Isosceles triangle","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7ee8-bfcc-d7284dfd6c4b","description":"Equilateral triangle","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7c19-9139-a34f563d0acb","description":"Scalene triangle","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7cdd-b50c-23d860392a27","description":"Rectangle","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7016-a83f-0699e17ae164","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which is NOT part of the water cycle?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Adherence describes molecules sticking to surfaces; percolation, evaporation, and precipitation describe water moving through the environment or changing state.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7a9d-a194-b7e81cf74d4b","description":"Adherence","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-76bf-951a-956f29e82182","description":"Percolation","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7194-b194-4c1663b4a574","description":"Evaporation","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-74ee-ae7e-fdce496f5826","description":"Precipitation","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7a17-831b-607c492fb567","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the symbol for Iron?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Fe comes from the Latin name ferrum. Iron is also the main metal in steel.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7c16-ab49-55e88090e205","description":"Fe","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7007-8599-62dd8b59c825","description":"Az","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-777b-8b43-08040e3020cc","description":"Ri","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7a5b-aa6a-fd186c23ada0","description":"Ir","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7608-af0b-3365e24c2f8a","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which mammal has the longest gestation period of any land animal, at around 22 months?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Elephants usually give birth to a single calf, which can stand and walk soon after birth.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7466-9e3f-d9fc34b06150","description":"Elephant","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7593-9e84-eea5c8b8c3e1","description":"Tiger","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-77b8-9d47-8084249ba6ff","description":"Hippopotamus","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7a18-a60e-59ba711398ba","description":"Giraffe","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7aa4-9e2d-8cb96c9028f9","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the chemical sodium chloride often used for?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Sodium chloride is table salt; concentrated salt draws water out of microbes, helping slow spoilage.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7e1e-99a3-502da1cfa20f","description":"It is commonly used as a condiment and food preservative.","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-75c9-8506-36ab8de6a6d7","description":"It is used to relieve pain.","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-71a6-aab5-deb092049fba","description":"It is used in thermometers, thermostats, barometers","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-713e-9fd7-60605e04e360","description":"It is used in nuclear reactors, as a neutron moderator.","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7eda-bbdd-4f9b6b2843ed","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which plant has bright yellow blossoms that turn into round, fluffy seed heads?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Each dandelion seed has a fine, parachute-like tuft that helps the wind carry it away.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7d98-907a-116dd83dd029","description":"Dandelion","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7ffc-ad1f-d2879e52ba2e","description":"Lily","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-744b-ad1f-bef9f197a67d","description":"Aster","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7e1f-8c4f-cffaf4b37d9a","description":"Common flax","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-7b49-8ae7-39986d6ce716","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"With which animals is the disease myxomatosis associated?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Myxomatosis is caused by the myxoma virus. Australia used it in the 1950s to reduce rabbit populations, though resistance later increased.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae83-75de-bb04-214b06e10e07","de