ed cutting the connections to and from the prefrontal cortex of the brain?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Lobotomy\u2019s developer, Ant\u00f3nio Egas Moniz, received the 1949 Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine for work on the therapeutic value of leucotomy.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-7d58-ab6e-7d44cb176c85","description":"Lobotomy","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-7db7-aede-d87feb1a49a7","description":"Electroconvulsive therapy","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-79d0-8db5-3f4643ee9f1d","description":"Insulin shock therapy","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-7863-8fbf-4e2805cf9120","description":"Trepanning","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-705e-86cd-74ac5ee5db32","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the name of the physical law that states that energy is neither created or destroyed?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The Law of Conservation of Energy says energy can change forms but the total remains constant in an isolated system.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-73f5-ac3e-4f0ddc54b80a","description":"Law of Conservation of Energy","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-78a4-be72-501329c03948","description":"Law of Universal Gravitation","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-757a-a123-6dbdfb1ee4d1","description":"Law of Thermodynamics","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-73e3-8369-bdf92a1000f0","description":"Law of the Lever","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-7697-92ec-9afa251c806f","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the streak of light called when a space rock burns up as it enters Earth\'s atmosphere?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"A meteor is the streak of light, often called a shooting star, made when a meteoroid burns up in the atmosphere.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-787c-a005-10d8d3cc9400","description":"Meteor","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-758e-8312-088a2cb5e4c1","description":"Comet","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-7225-a6ef-e4f172965432","description":"Pulsar","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-7549-a77f-17761996bba0","description":"Aurora","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-7559-b574-486a27519afb","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the study of human beings and their cultures?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Anthropology is often divided into cultural, biological, linguistic, and archaeological branches, which study humans from different perspectives.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-7d33-bab4-951b3b9d99c5","description":"Anthropology","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-776d-a82e-a43c4c0fcac5","description":"Anthology","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-7dd3-9715-169402bade5c","description":"Geography","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-7dcd-aa68-727c6045dcdd","description":"Apiology","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-72f2-93c0-122cd75db8c6","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the name of the soil that is always frozen and helps to define the boundary of the Arctic?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Permafrost is ground that remains at or below freezing for at least two consecutive years; a seasonally thawed active layer can sit above it.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-7e37-990d-efb252447170","description":"Permafrost","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-7016-93b3-322ebb7d2670","description":"Icerock","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-70ea-b6d1-3efc31d3dd75","description":"Coolground","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-7b7c-8bc1-ff1fa02561d2","description":"Evercold","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-7367-8938-e64f30c67b96","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which of these is a popular programming language?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Java was developed at Sun Microsystems and became widely known for runnin