swer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-7901-95ab-af3b484b1662","description":"7 \u00d7 6 = 42","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-78ed-b8b9-76ae301d42f1","description":"9 \u00d7 7 = 63","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-78a2-a567-2fc670ac5294","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is Coniology the study of?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Coniology is the study of atmospheric dust and its effects; its name derives from the Greek word konis, meaning dust.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-7e7a-9a6f-554ea352bca5","description":"Atmospheric dust and its effects","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-7583-ac08-7bed4c378659","description":"Life","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-7c5b-b646-2231f6f4d298","description":"Human culture","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-7141-8ba0-05386835da8e","description":"Dogs","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-78f5-909d-384d8cb553c5","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the name of the dinosaur that had a large sail-like structure on its back?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Spinosaurus means \u201cspine lizard,\u201d referring to the long spines along its back that supported the sail.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-78a1-9a2a-60c108502ca8","description":"Spinosaurus","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-7ce3-9009-1c0b77725b9c","description":"Triceratops","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-7f4e-bc36-48c58ee354f8","description":"Stegosaurus","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-7b4b-a025-118a20bd36dc","description":"Diplodocus","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-7563-b290-2f3d91b3256e","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is Symbology the study of?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Symbology examines how emblems and images convey meaning; heraldry, for example, gives colors and figures on coats of arms particular associations.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-79da-98ea-f8edf6527e0a","description":"the study and interpretation of symbols, or a set of symbols","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-7604-9730-15c07b41e535","description":"the structure of cells","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-78a1-9682-2f247ea8a5f3","description":"the process of biological evolution","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-7abf-8b6b-83a4646d9b9b","description":"reptiles and amphibians","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-7ecd-9431-0d886972a90d","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What term describes a computer-generated 3D environment that a user can interact with as if it were real?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Virtual reality typically uses a headset to replace the user\'s view of their surroundings with a computer-generated scene; augmented reality adds digital elements to the real world.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-7c01-8964-950c1f42b364","description":"Virtual reality","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-7cbf-b3e0-feb7c218becb","description":"Augmented reality","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-7964-a34b-534a43924d2b","description":"Mixed media","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-7596-9643-c4fe634e255b","description":"Digital hologram","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-7f68-8c0f-475733bd3a7d","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which dwarf planet is the only one located in the asteroid belt between Mars and Jupiter?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Ceres was discovered by Giuseppe Piazzi in 1801 and was initially classified as a planet before later being designated a dwarf planet.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-77db-a15f-489f54af926a","description":"Ceres","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-7ad1-b60c-b9bc4af5e926","description":"Eris","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-7ae6-96b0-02043d9f8e4f","description":"Haumea","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-