owed the vaccine\u2019s effectiveness: the vaccinated sheep survived exposure to anthrax, while the unvaccinated sheep died.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-76a4-bf16-370c9181269d","description":"Louis Pasteur","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-7c22-9d00-5b7ce5a08690","description":"Robert Koch","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-78c5-b8fc-7408b8ed0644","description":"Edward Jenner","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-7100-bd52-aa9c3c698c50","description":"Alexander Fleming","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-7560-b14b-da5511c915e6","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What name is given to the single super-continent that existed 200 million years ago?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Pangaea began breaking apart as tectonic plates shifted, eventually separating into the continents we know today.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-7d38-a1ec-a2e6d5a33be0","description":"Pangaea","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-7e9a-92e3-334840ff0b16","description":"Laurasia","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-7fe3-85d8-fb1901c2403f","description":"Rodinia","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-7b04-bbd3-5768411b4596","description":"Gondwana","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-70d4-a22e-c964ea872c38","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the name given to a poison that acts on the nervous system?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Neurotoxins affect nerve cells or their signaling. Botulinum toxin is one example; it disrupts communication between nerves and muscles.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-7cdc-84c8-c0c604440cae","description":"Neurotoxins","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-7845-ba1c-d216a5b82d47","description":"Neurovenoms","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-73ce-bbcf-f731f3c3bf2e","description":"Endotoxins","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a2190a-ae84-79c0-909b-09926ac83add","description":"Endovenoms","correct_